      "writtenOn": "2023-06-14T20:06:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I said above, we should take all reasonable precautions. Yes there are still races but those are tighter and much harder to fix. The additional delay introduced by waiting on the modem widens the window for this to happen. As you said, responding correctly to the UNFROZEN event will mitigate the race, shrinking the window back down to \u0027we raced unfreeze with SOCK_DESTROY\u0027.\n\nI really don\u0027t want to argue the intent of the previous patch (it was changed significantly, if you recall). I\u0027m also not interested in arguing about existing races that can\u0027t be fixed yet. The freezer timeout is irrelevant here - it\u0027s the user who brings apps to the foreground.\n\nYou widened the window for us to race teardown with unfreeze, and I\u0027m simply asking you to please shrink it back down.",
      "parentUuid": "eda6076a_66ea0548",
      "revId": "c4d1da75e775467503c95453cdadf0edbc85eceb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
